    "title": "Concept 1: Median from cumulative frequency graph",
    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">The median is the middle value of a data set. On a cumulative frequency graph, you find it by locating half the total frequency, then reading horizontally to the curve and dropping vertically to the x-axis to read the median value.</p>",
