    "title": "Concept 2: Quartiles from cumulative frequency graph",
    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Quartiles divide the data into four equal parts. The lower quartile (Q1) corresponds to n/4 total frequency, and the upper quartile (Q3) corresponds to 3n/4 total frequency. We find these by reading across from the frequency axis to the curve and then down to the x-axis.</p>",
